v0.10.20: legacy agent-slug audit + rename — heal the existing data

The follow-up v0.10.16 named explicitly and deferred:

  Not in scope (v0.10.17 candidate):
    - Rename migration for the un-routable data already in the DB.
      abw-cli agents legacy-slugs --dry-run / --apply. Same
      invariant, different verb (heal existing data vs guard new
      writes).

v0.10.16 closed the creation-time bypasses. This heals the 43 rows
already in `agents` — Mario's efra-ai/04-forensic and siblings.
Un-routable because axum's tree router splits on `/`, so
/agent/efra-ai/04-forensic never matches /agent/:name; names with
`-` also fail slug::validate on any later write.

1. GET|POST /api/admin/agents/legacy-slugs

   src/handlers/admin.rs — admin_legacy_agent_slugs_handler

   One handler, two modes via `apply` (default false):
     GET  …/legacy-slugs              audit only
     POST …/legacy-slugs              audit only
     POST …/legacy-slugs?apply=true   execute

   Identical response shape in both modes — only action_taken
   differs per row — so a dry run is a faithful preview.

   Renames run in a transaction and backfill the JSONB refs in
   fermi_forecasts.agents_used so renamed agents don't orphan the
   forecasts citing them. Every rename lands in admin_bypass_events
   (the v0.10.5 table) with the old → new mapping.

   Platform-admin gated at the route, so `apply` needs no extra
   permission check.

2. sanitise_legacy_agent_name

   slug::validate is reject-only; apps::workspace_fork::slugify is
   private to its module. Neither reusable, so a conservative
   sanitiser scoped to this handler:

     * lowercase ASCII letters, keep digits + underscores
     * every other char (-, /, ., space) → single _, runs collapsed
     * strip leading digits/underscores (slugs start with a letter)
     * strip trailing _, truncate to 64
     * None below 3 chars, or on collision with a reserved slug —
       flagged for manual review rather than guessed at

   Output satisfies slug::validate when Some; caller re-validates.

3. abw-cli admin legacy-slugs

   crates/abw-cli/src/commands/admin.rs (new) + registration in
   commands/mod.rs and main.rs. Runs the audit from a terminal
   without hand-rolling curl against an admin token.

No migration. Endpoint is inert until called with ?apply=true.
Run the dry run first — unrecoverable names are reported, not
silently skipped.

Related:
  v0.10.5   admin_bypass_events (the audit table reused here)
  v0.10.16  closed the creation-time bypasses producing this data
  d0f94e8   slug::validate introduced 2026-05-23; everything
            created before that date was unchecked
